course: dictionary
lesson: 922
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The same word can have different meanings in different places. To find the right one, read the words around it. «Press firmly on the wound with a clean cloth to stop the bleeding.» The wound and the cloth are your clues: bleeding means losing blood from a cut.
explain: «Painting on wet paper so the colours spread is called wet-on-wet.» Here the clue is colours spreading. Bleeding can also mean spreading from one area into another, like wet paint. Ask: does my meaning fit? Losing blood would not make sense for paint, so the paint meaning is the right one.
explain: Some words are about feelings or pictures in your head, but bleeding here is simple and physical. When you meet a word with more than one meaning, test each meaning in the sentence and keep the one that makes sense.
fact: Bleeding means losing blood from a cut, wound or injury.
fact: Bleeding can be a noun too: it is the flow of blood from the body, as in a bleeding nose.
fact: For a cut, press firmly with a clean cloth, raise the injured part if you can, and get an adult. Serious bleeding needs emergency help.
fact: For a nosebleed, sit up, lean forward and pinch the soft part of the nose.
fact: In colours, bleeding means spreading from one area into another, like wet paint or dye.
exercise: «Press firmly on the wound with a clean cloth to stop the bleeding.» What does bleeding mean here? | Going dry and stiff | *Losing blood from a cut | Shouting very loudly | Spreading colours on wet paper
exercise: Ellie's paint is bleeding into the blue. What does bleeding mean here? | Losing blood from a cut | *Spreading from one area into another | Drying very quickly | Being very loud
exercise: «It's just a scratch» about a cut that won't stop bleeding is a bad idea. What should you do instead? | Ignore it because it is only a scratch | Paint a picture of it | Wait for it to dry, like paint | *Press with a clean cloth and get an adult
test: Sam has a bleeding nose. What should he do first? | *Sit up, lean forward and pinch the soft part of his nose | Rub his nose hard with his hand | Run outside into the cold air | Lie flat on his back and tilt his head back
test: Which word is the noun for the flow of blood from the body? | *bleeding | bleeds | bled | bleed
exam: «Ladybirds bleed a bitter, smelly yellow liquid from their knees when attacked.» Which meaning of bleeding fits this sentence? | *Losing blood or fluid from the body | Spreading from one area into another | Going soft and wet like dough | Being very loud
